<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    C054 verify target: dotnet test backend/src/Ocr.Api.Tests -c Release

    Real Postgres, real OpenCV, real Tesseract, and a recording HTTP server standing in for Gemini.
    Every one of this component's definition-of-done items is a claim about something outside the
    process, and three of them are claims about pixels:

      * "no unredacted image is sent to the external model in an integration test with a network
        recorder" is asserted on the BYTES the recorder captured — their sha256 is the redacted
        artefact's, it is not the raw file's, and the raw file's hash appears nowhere in the request.
      * "with Gemini unavailable the Tesseract path still produces fields" runs the real `tesseract`
        binary over a real rendered document, with the stub answering 503.
      * "a low-confidence field is written pending and never auto-verified" and "a plate mismatch
        marks the photos step pending_review" are driven through the stub's own answers, because
        reproducing them against the real model would mean carrying deliberately blurry photographs
        in the repository and hoping it stays as unsure of them as it is today.

    The document fixtures are RENDERED with OpenCV rather than checked in: a binary fixture is
    opaque in review, and one whose text nobody can read from the diff is a poor thing to hang a
    redaction assertion on. `DocumentFixtures` is the whole vocabulary.

    NATIVE DEPENDENCIES. This suite needs `tesseract` on PATH, OpenCV's native library
    (libgtk-3-0t64 + libatomic1 on Debian/Ubuntu) and a Haar cascade (`opencv-data`). CI installs
    all three on the backend leg; see backend/src/Ocr.Api/CLAUDE.md. Where one is missing the
    service degrades fail-closed rather than crashing, and the tests that assert THAT are the ones
    that still run.

    No Redis, no Kafka, no bearer: the service holds none of them, deliberately (see OcrApplication).

    Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web, not Microsoft.NET.Sdk: the harness builds two WebApplications — the
    service and the Gemini recorder.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.Ocr.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <!--
      xUnit1041: collection-fixture ctor args are consumed through the primary constructor.
      xUnit1051: every test is bounded by its own harness lifetime.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);xUnit1041;xUnit1051</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" />
    <PackageReference Include="Dapper" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" />
    <!-- The document fixtures are drawn, not checked in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenCvSharp4" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenCvSharp4.official.runtime.linux-x64" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Ocr.Api\Ocr.Api.csproj" />
    <!-- C010: the Postgres fixture, so this suite runs the same server build the dev stack does
         and applies the same migration set — including 1310's processing-log columns. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MageRide.TestKit\MageRide.TestKit.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
